reading: a positive Weil inf-floor at fixed a<1, roughly band-flat (ratio ~O(1)), is the
empirical form of the OPEN uniform sub-critical bound (§370). If the Weil floor is band-flat
where the overlap floor is too, the arithmetic rides the frame geometry uniformly — the
uniform bound would then reduce to the (open but concrete) frame-theoretic one.
